  "title": "1991 eruption of Mount Pinatubo",
  "summary": "Mount Pinatubo on Luzon erupted on 15 June 1991, sending an ash cloud 35 kilometers high and ejecting more than 5 cubic kilometers of material. USGS calls it the second-largest eruption of the century; forecasts and evacuations saved at least 5,000 lives. Deaths are put at about 300 to 400 by Earth magazine and more than 840 by USGS. Global temperatures fell about 0.5 C in 1991-93.",
